---
const layouts = [
  {name:'Three in North',counts:[3,0,0]},
  {name:'Two North, one West',counts:[2,1,0]},
  {name:'One per region',counts:[1,1,1]},
  {name:'Five: two, two, one',counts:[2,2,1]},
].map(layout=>({...layout,total:layout.counts.reduce((a,b)=>a+b,0),majority:Math.floor(layout.counts.reduce((a,b)=>a+b,0)/2)+1}));
const regions=['North','West','East'];
---
<figure class="placement-figure wide" data-placement-quorum aria-labelledby="placement-quorum-title">
  <figcaption id="placement-quorum-title"><span>Figure 1</span> <strong>Remove a domain, then count the voters</strong></figcaption>
  <div class="placement-panel">
    <div class="placement-options">
      <label>Voting layout <select data-layout>{layouts.map((layout,i)=><option value={i} selected={i===0}>{layout.name}</option>)}</select></label>
      <label>Failure <select data-failure>
        <option value="none">None</option><option value="zone">North zone 1 lost</option>
        <option value="North">North lost</option><option value="West">West lost</option><option value="East">East lost</option>
        <option value="split">North isolated</option>
      </select></label>
    </div>
    <div class="placement-regions" aria-label="Voters by region">
      {regions.map((region,r)=><div class="placement-region" data-region={region}>
        <b>{region}</b>
        {[0,1,2].map(z=><div class="placement-zone" data-zone={`${r}-${z}`} hidden={r!==0}>
          <span>Zone {z+1}</span><strong data-voter data-live>{r===0 ? `N${z+1} · voter` : 'No voter'}</strong>
        </div>)}
      </div>)}
    </div>
    <p class="placement-result" data-count data-live>3 surviving voters · majority 2 of 3</p>
    <p class="placement-explanation" data-explanation data-live aria-live="polite">All three voters can communicate. The group can form its required majority of two.</p>
  </div>
  <p class="placement-caption">Each voter occupies a different machine in its own zone. Empty zones are omitted when the layout changes. “North isolated” leaves North separate from a communicating West–East side. Counts assume the remaining voters and storage work, and allow any necessary election; they do not promise immediate service.</p>
  <details><summary>All layouts and region-loss counts as text</summary>
    <div class="table-scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Region loss voter counts"><table>
      <caption>Communicating voters remaining after one whole region is lost</caption>
      <thead><tr><th scope="col">Layout</th><th scope="col">Majority</th><th scope="col">North lost</th><th scope="col">West lost</th><th scope="col">East lost</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>{layouts.map(layout=><tr><th scope="row">{layout.name}</th><td>{layout.majority}</td>{layout.counts.map(c=><td>{layout.total-c} · {layout.total-c>=layout.majority?'passes':'no majority'}</td>)}</tr>)}</tbody>
    </table></div>
    <p>Losing North zone 1 removes one voter in every layout. North isolated: three in North can continue only on North’s side; two in North can continue only on North’s side; one per region can continue only on West–East’s side; five placed two–two–one can continue only on West–East’s side. The application must reach the side with a majority.</p>
  </details>
</figure>
<script>
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-placement-quorum]').forEach(root=>{
    const layouts=[[3,0,0],[2,1,0],[1,1,1],[2,2,1]];
    const regions=['North','West','East'];
    const layout=root.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-layout]')!;
    const failure=root.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-failure]')!;
    const draw=()=>{
      const counts=layouts[Number(layout.value)];
      const n=counts.reduce((a,b)=>a+b,0), q=Math.floor(n/2)+1;
      let alive=0;
      regions.forEach((region,r)=>{
        for(let z=0;z<3;z++){
          const zone=root.querySelector<HTMLElement>(`[data-zone="${r}-${z}"]`)!;
          const exists=z<counts[r];
          zone.hidden=!exists;
          const lost=failure.value===region||(failure.value==='zone'&&r===0&&z===0);
          zone.classList.toggle('is-lost',lost);
          zone.querySelector('[data-voter]')!.textContent=`${region[0]}${z+1} · ${lost?'lost':'voter'}`;
          if(exists&&!lost) alive++;
        }
        const box=root.querySelector<HTMLElement>(`[data-region="${region}"]`)!;
        box.classList.toggle('is-isolated',failure.value==='split'&&r===0);
        let empty=box.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-empty]');
        if(!empty){empty=document.createElement('p');empty.dataset.empty='';empty.textContent='No voters';box.append(empty);}
        empty.hidden=counts[r]>0;
      });
      const split=failure.value==='split';
      const largest=split?Math.max(counts[0],counts[1]+counts[2]):alive;
      root.querySelector('[data-count]')!.textContent=split
        ?`North: ${counts[0]} · West–East: ${counts[1]+counts[2]} · majority ${q} of ${n}`
        :`${alive} surviving ${alive===1?'voter':'voters'} · majority ${q} of ${n}`;
      const side=counts[0]>=q?'North':'West–East';
      root.querySelector('[data-explanation]')!.textContent=split
        ?`${side} has a communicating majority. The other side cannot agree new writes. A request must reach ${side}; the configured group still has ${n} voters.`
        :largest>=q?`The ${alive} surviving voters can communicate and reach the required ${q}. New writes have a quorum path, after any necessary election.`
        :`Only ${alive} ${alive===1?'voter remains':'voters remain'}, fewer than the required ${q}. Retained copies cannot agree new writes. The configured majority does not shrink after a failure.`;
    };
    layout.addEventListener('change',draw);failure.addEventListener('change',draw);draw();
  });
</script>
